    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe old membership *tier* was a derived string getter (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) on `Owner`. The spec asked for a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) assigned **on creation**, so I made it a stored, pipeline-assigned field following the same pattern the other create-time attributes (`customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `namesakeCount`) already use.\n\n**Domain model** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`\n- Added the persisted `membershipLevel` field with getter/setter.\n- Removed `getMembershipTier()` and its now-unused `StringUtils` import.\n\n**New create-pipeline step** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipLevel.java`\n- Single-responsibility function: start at 1, +1 for an email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 explicitly reserved for tenure). Computed inline in the function, mirroring `AssignMembershipNumber`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`\n- Inserted `assignMembershipLevel` after `countNamesakes` (so the namesake count is set) and before `save` (so it's persisted), under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n**Audit** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`\n- The create audit line now records `membershipLevel` alongside id/customerCode/registrationDate (verified in the run: `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 ... membershipLevel=3`).\n\n**Response contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`\n- Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) property with `membershipLevel` (int32, 1\u20134, level 4 reserved). MapStruct auto-maps `owner.getMembershipLevel()` into the generated DTO by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n**Schema** \u2014 `db/{h2,hsqldb,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`\n- Added the `membership_level` column to each `owners` table (tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL is required there).\n\n## Notes / decisions\n- I made `membershipLevel` a **stored** field rather than a derived getter because the spec frames it as assigned \"on creation\" and reserves level 4 for tenure \u2014 a stored value is what a future tenure step could bump.\n- I left `householdSize`/`CountHouseholdMembers` in place. They previously fed only the dropped `GOLD` rule, but they persist a real recorded attribute; removing the column/step/schema is outside this change's scope and riskier than warranted.\n\n## Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (`AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` asserts `$.membershipLevel == 3` for an owner with an email and no namesakes).",
